  "strategy": "control",
  "colors": "GUR",
  "identity": "Three-colour Vivid control. Every payoff in this deck reads the same variable - X, 'the number of colors among permanents you control' - and the deck's whole construction is a machine for inflating that one number. Prismatic Undercurrents is the lands-matter keystone: it grants an additional land drop every turn AND searches for X basic lands, so the same counter that sizes the threats also sizes the mana. The trick that makes a three-colour deck reach X=5 is that lands are colourless permanents, so raising X is not about playing more colours of cards - Shimmerwilds Growth reads 'Enchanted land IS the chosen color' and paints a land a colour you do not otherwise play, Puca's Eye 'becomes the chosen color', and Tam sets the count to 5 on demand. At X=5 Wildvine Pummeler costs {1}{G} for a 6/5 reach trample, Squawkroaster is a 5/4 double striker, Shinestriker draws five, and Prismabasher gives up to five creatures +5/+5.",
  "restrictions": {
